PROJECT: Blast

## Strategic Objectives

Strategic Objective: Launch Ethereum L2 Optimistic Rollup dengan native yield sebagai diferensiasi utama  
Evidence: Launch blog menyatakan "Blast is an Ethereum L2 with native yield" sebagai value proposition utama (HIGH) [Blast Blog Introducing Blast, https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast]  
Evidence: Arsitektur NativeYieldPrecompile (0x4300...0004) di-deploy sejak genesis mainnet untuk rebasing otomatis yield L1 ke user L2 (HIGH) [Blastscan NativeYieldPrecompile, https://blastscan.io/address/0x4300000000000000000000000000000000000004]  
Sources: https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast, https://blastscan.io/address/0x4300000000000000000000000000000000000004

Strategic Objective: Bootstrap liquidity dan user base melalui Points/Gold incentive program sebelum TGE  
Evidence: Points Season 1 dimulai Nov 2023 (pre-mainnet) untuk deposit ke bridge; Gold program untuk builder protokol (HIGH) [Blast Blog Introducing Blast, https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast]  
Evidence: 25.5% token allocation ke Community (Points), 28% ke Ecosystem (Gold) — total 53.5% untuk insentif ekosistem (HIGH) [Blast Blog TGE, https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event]  
Sources: https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast, https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event

Strategic Objective: Integrate dengan Blur NFT ecosystem untuk liquidity dan user crossover  
Evidence: Founder Tieshun Roquerre adalah co-founder Blur; launch blog menyebut "Blur integration" sebagai bagian ekosistem (HIGH) [Blast Blog Introducing Blast, https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast]  
Evidence: Blur tercantum di Entity Phase 2 sebagai Company external dengan fungsi Application, Liquidity, Distribution (HIGH) [Phase 2 Entity: Blur]  
Sources: https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast, Phase 2 Entity: Blur

Strategic Objective: Achieve progressive decentralization via DAO governance post-TGE  
Evidence: TGE blog menyatakan governance akan diaktifkan via BLAST token; 10% Foundation + 28% Ecosystem allocation dikelola via governance (HIGH) [Blast Blog TGE, https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event]  
Evidence: Governance model tercantum di Phase 6: token-weighted voting, delegation supported, Foundation multisig execution (HIGH) [Phase 6 Governance section]  
Sources: https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event, Phase 6 Governance section

## Decision Timeline

Decision: Establish Blast Foundation di Cayman Islands sebagai entitas hukum  
Date: 2023-11-20 (sebelum announcement)  
Trigger: Perlu legal wrapper untuk token issuance, treasury management, dan compliance sebelum public launch  
Evidence: Founding Entity: Blast Foundation (Cayman Islands) di announcement blog (HIGH) [Blast Blog Introducing Blast, https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast]  
Immediate Result: Entitas legal siap untuk funding round dan token generation  
Long-term Impact: Menentukan jurisdiksi regulasi, struktur DAO wrapper, dan liability framework  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-001  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 1 Foundation, Phase 2 Entity: Blast Foundation, Phase 3 EV-001

Decision: Raise strategic funding dari Paradigm dan Standard Crypto  
Date: 2023-11  
Trigger: Capital requirement untuk tim 50+ orang, infrastructure, dan go-to-market sebelum mainnet  
Evidence: Media reports (The Block, CoinDesk) menyebut $20M–$30M; blog resmi tidak disclose amount (MEDIUM) [The Block, https://www.theblock.co/post/264000/blur-founder-launches-blast-ethereum-layer-2]  
Immediate Result: Runway untuk mainnet launch Feb 2024; investor allocation 16.5% token supply  
Long-term Impact: Investor vesting schedule undisclosed menciptakan overhang risk; strategic guidance dari top-tier VC  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-003  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-003, Phase 5 Funding History, Phase 6 Distribution

Decision: Launch testnet dengan Points Season 1 sebelum mainnet  
Date: 2023-11-21  
Trigger: Need pre-mainnet TVL, user base, dan sybil-resistant distribution mechanism untuk TGE  
Evidence: Points program announced同日 dengan testnet launch; bridge deposits open Nov 2023 (HIGH) [Blast Blog Introducing Blast, https://blog.blast.io/introducing-blast]  
Immediate Result: Ratusan juta USD TVL di bridge pre-mainnet; >500k unique addresses (blog claim)  
Long-term Impact: Community expectation untuk airdrop; TVL decline post-Season 1 snapshot (DefiLlama shows peak Mar 2024 then decline)  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-002, EV-004  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-002/EV-004, Phase 8 Adoption Metrics (TVL peak $1.48B Mar 2024)

Decision: Deploy mainnet dengan centralized sequencer dan permissioned proposer/challenger  
Date: 2024-02-29  
Trigger: Time-to-market priority; OP Stack fault proof components ready tapi decentralized sequencer/challenger belum mature  
Evidence: Mainnet launch blog; GitHub contracts menunjukkan single sequencer address, permissioned L2OutputOracle/DisputeGame (HIGH) [Blast Blog Mainnet Launch, https://blog.blast.io/blast-mainnet-launch] [Blast GitHub L2OutputOracle, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/L2OutputOracle.sol]  
Immediate Result: Mainnet live dengan native yield active; 7-day withdrawal via canonical bridge  
Long-term Impact: Centralization criticism; roadmap decentralization tidak dipublikasikan; censorship/liveness risk  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-006  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-006, Phase 4 Core Components (Sequencer/Proposer/Challenger), Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks

Decision: Activate native yield dari Lido stETH dan MakerDAO Spark USDS sejak genesis  
Date: 2024-02-29  
Trigger: Core differentiator "native yield" harus live day-1 untuk memvalidasi value prop  
Evidence: NativeYieldPrecompile active block 1; yield sources documented di docs (HIGH) [Blastscan NativeYieldPrecompile, https://blastscan.io/address/0x4300000000000000000000000000000000000004] [Blast Docs Native Yield, https://docs.blast.io/native-yield]  
Immediate Result: Semua address L2 menerima rebasing yield otomatis tanpa staking  
Long-term Impact: Protocol dependency pada Lido + MakerDAO; oracle dependency pada Chainlink; yield rate transparency gap  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-006  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 4 Native Yield Distributor, Phase 7 External Dependencies (Lido, MakerDAO, Chainlink), Phase 8 Narrative Position

Decision: Conduct TGE dengan 100B fixed supply, 53.5% ke community/ecosystem, no public sale  
Date: 2024-06-26  
Trigger: Token utility untuk governance, staking, fee payment; reward early participants (Points S1); fund ecosystem growth (Gold)  
Evidence: TGE blog detail allocation: Community 25.5%, Ecosystem 28%, Team 20%, Investors 16.5%, Foundation 10% (HIGH) [Blast Blog TGE, https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event]  
Immediate Result: Token tradeable di 4 major CEX + native DEX; Season 1 claim live; governance activated  
Long-term Impact: High FDV vs low float (vesting undisclosed); no buyback/burn mechanism; inflation only via allocated supply emissions  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-012, EV-013  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-012/EV-013, Phase 6 Token Information/Distribution/Vesting, Phase 8 Trading Markets

Decision: Launch Blast Points Season 2 dengan mekanisme expanded (on-chain activity, bukan hanya deposit)  
Date: 2024-07  
Trigger: Retain users post-TGE; drive DEX volume, lending activity, social engagement (Kaito)  
Evidence: Season 2 announcement Jul 2024; mechanics expanded beyond bridge deposits (HIGH) [Blast Blog, https://blog.blast.io] [Phase 3 EV-014]  
Immediate Result: On-chain activity increase (DEX volume, lending, social); Gold distributions ongoing ke Thruster/Ring/Wasabi/Kaito  
Long-term Impact: Season 2 ended Dec 2024 (EV-019); Season 3 mechanics unannounced; retention dependency pada incentives  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-014, EV-008/009/010/011  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-014/EV-019, Phase 7 Major Integrations/Applications, Phase 8 Adoption Metrics

Decision: Execute Blast v1.1 hard fork untuk performance, fee market tuning, EIP-2612 permit  
Date: 2024-11  
Trigger: Scaling needs (block time 2s→1s), gas fee stability, UX improvement untuk BLAST token (gasless approval)  
Evidence: GitHub release v1.1.0; blog announcement Nov 2024 (MEDIUM) [Blast GitHub Release v1.1, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/releases/tag/v1.1.0] [Blast Blog, https://blog.blast.io]  
Immediate Result: Throughput increase; EIP-1559 parameters tuned; BLAST permit enabled untuk staking/governance UX  
Long-term Impact: Demonstrates upgrade capability via Foundation multisig; governance execution still centralized  
Related Historical Event ID: EV-018  
Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-018, Phase 4 Technical Upgrade History, Phase 6 Utility (Fee Payment)

## Evolution Pattern

Strategy Evolution: Pre-launch stealth → Public announcement dengan Points program → Mainnet launch dengan native yield → TGE dengan exchange listings → Incentive seasons (S1→S2) → Protocol upgrades (v1.1)  
Evidence: Timeline Phase 3 menunjukkan progression: EV-001 (announcement) → EV-002/004 (testnet+Points) → EV-006 (mainnet) → EV-012/013 (TGE) → EV-014 (S2) → EV-018 (upgrade) → EV-019 (S2 end) (HIGH) [Phase 3 Event Dataset]  
Sources: Phase 3 Event Dataset

Technology Evolution: OP Stack fork (DisputeGame, L2OutputOracle) → Custom NativeYieldPrecompile → blast-geth execution client → EIP-4844 blob adoption → v1.1 hard fork (EIP-1559 tuning, EIP-2612)  
Evidence: GitHub contracts berbasis OP Stack fault proof; NativeYieldPrecompile custom; blob support docs; v1.1 release notes (HIGH) [Phase 4 Core Components, Technical Upgrade History, GitHub Contracts]  
Sources: Phase 4 Technical Upgrade History, Phase 4 Core Components, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts

Tokenomics Evolution: Fixed 100B supply minted genesis → TGE unlock Community S1 (100%) → Ongoing emissions via Points S2+ dan Gold (vesting undisclosed) → Staking/governance/fee utility activated post-TGE → Permit (EIP-2612) added v1.1  
Evidence: Phase 6 Supply/Distribution/Vesting/TGE/Utility sections; v1.1 permit addition (HIGH) [Phase 6 all sections, Phase 4 EV-018]  
Sources: Phase 6 Token Information, Distribution, Vesting Schedule, TGE, Utility, Phase 4 EV-018

Governance Evolution: Foundation-controlled (multisig upgrade keys, permissioned proposer/challenger) → TGE token-weighted voting activated → DAO formation projected 2025 (EV-020) → No council/committee structure yet  
Evidence: Phase 2 Entity: Blast Foundation; Phase 4 Security Model (upgrade control); Phase 6 Governance; Phase 3 EV-020 (projected) (HIGH) [Phase 2, Phase 4, Phase 6, Phase 3 EV-020]  
Sources: Phase 2 Entity: Blast Foundation, Phase 4 Security Model, Phase 6 Governance, Phase 3 EV-020

Ecosystem Evolution: Blur integration (founder connection) → Core DeFi trio launch (Thruster DEX, Ring Lending, Wasabi Options) Mar-Apr 2024 → Kaito InfoFi integration May 2024 → Third-party bridges (LayerZero, Wormhole, Orbiter) → Hackathons/Grants (Gold program, Ecosystem Fund Q4 2024)  
Evidence: Phase 3 EV-008/009/010/011; Phase 7 Major Integrations/Applications/Infrastructure Providers/Developer Ecosystem (HIGH) [Phase 3, Phase 7]  
Sources: Phase 3 EV-008/009/010/011, Phase 7 Major Integrations, Applications, Infrastructure Providers, Developer Ecosystem

## Technical Decision Pattern

Decision: Choose Optimistic Rollup (OP Stack fault proof) over ZK Rollup  
Reason: Faster time-to-market; EVM equivalence easier; OP Stack battle-tested (Optimism, Base); native yield implementation simpler pada optimistic model  
Evidence: Architecture docs describe Optimistic Rollup dengan 7-day challenge; DisputeGame menggunakan Cannon/MIPS dari OP Stack (HIGH) [Blast Docs Architecture, https://docs.blast.io/architecture] [Blast GitHub DisputeGame, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/DisputeGame.sol]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/architecture, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/DisputeGame.sol

Decision: Implement native yield via custom precompile (0x4300...0004) rebasing mechanism bukan ERC-4626 vault  
Reason: Gas efficiency (rebasing per block tanpa user tx); automatic untuk semua address (no opt-in); composability dengan existing DeFi (token balance increases natively)  
Evidence: NativeYieldPrecompile adalah ERC-20 precompile dengan rebasing logic; docs describe "automatic yield to all addresses" (HIGH) [Blast Docs Native Yield Technical, https://docs.blast.io/native-yield/technical-details] [Blastscan NativeYieldPrecompile, https://blastscan.io/address/0x4300000000000000000000000000000000000004]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/native-yield/technical-details, https://blastscan.io/address/0x4300000000000000000000000000000000000004

Decision: Use centralized sequencer (single) dengan roadmap ke decentralization unspecified  
Reason: Simplicity, low latency, deterministic ordering untuk launch; decentralized sequencer (shared/BoLD) masih R&D di industry  
Evidence: Docs state "single sequencer operated by Foundation"; no forced inclusion contract found in GitHub (HIGH) [Blast Docs Sequencer, https://docs.blast.io/architecture/sequencer] [Blast GitHub Contracts, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/architecture/sequencer, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts

Decision: Keep proposer/challenger permissioned (Foundation whitelist)  
Reason: Safety during early mainnet; fraud proof system (Cannon) complex; permissionless challenge game requires more testing  
Evidence: L2OutputOracle dan DisputeGame contracts have owner/whitelist access control; no permissionless challenge game live (HIGH) [Blast GitHub L2OutputOracle, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/L2OutputOracle.sol] [Blast GitHub DisputeGame, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/DisputeGame.sol]  
Sources: https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/L2OutputOracle.sol, https://github.com/blastL2/contracts/blob/main/src/L1/DisputeGame.sol

Decision: Depend on Chainlink price feeds untuk yield oracle (stETH/ETH, USDS/USD)  
Reason: Chainlink is industry standard, battle-tested, decentralized oracle network; no need to build custom oracle  
Evidence: Docs describe yield rate oracle menggunakan Chainlink feeds; no fallback oracle documented (MEDIUM) [Blast Docs Native Yield Oracle, https://docs.blast.io/native-yield/oracle]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/native-yield/oracle

Decision: Not open-source execution client (blast-geth)  
Reason: Competitive advantage? Security through obscurity? Not disclosed. Industry trend: OP Stack clients open source (op-geth), but Blast custom fork may have proprietary optimizations  
Evidence: GitHub org blastL2 has contracts, SDK, but no blast-geth repo visible (LOW) [Blast GitHub Org, https://github.com/blastL2]  
Sources: https://github.com/blastL2

Decision: Canonical bridge only supports token transfer (ETH, ERC-20, ERC-721), no arbitrary messaging  
Reason: Simpler security model; arbitrary messaging adds complexity and attack surface; third-party protocols (LayerZero, Wormhole) fill this gap  
Evidence: Bridge docs state "native bridge only supports token transfer"; third-party bridges listed separately (HIGH) [Blast Docs Bridge, https://docs.blast.io/bridge]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/bridge

## Financial Decision Pattern

Decision: Raise single strategic round dari Paradigm + Standard Crypto (~$20-30M) tanpa public sale  
Reason: Top-tier VC validation; strategic value beyond capital (network, recruitment, credibility); avoid regulatory complexity of public sale; maintain control via Foundation  
Evidence: Media reports only; blog silent on amount; investor allocation 16.5% token supply (MEDIUM) [The Block, https://www.theblock.co/post/264000/blur-founder-launches-blast-ethereum-layer-2] [CoinDesk, https://www.coindesk.com/business/2023/11/20/blur-founder-launches-blast-ethereum-layer-2] [Phase 6 Distribution]  
Sources: https://www.theblock.co/post/264000/blur-founder-launches-blast-ethereum-layer-2, https://www.coindesk.com/business/2023/11/20/blur-founder-launches-blast-ethereum-layer-2, Phase 6 Distribution

Decision: Allocate 53.5% token supply ke Community (25.5%) + Ecosystem (28%) — very high vs typical L2 (Arbitrum ~12% community, Optimism ~19% retroPGF+ecosystem)  
Reason: Aggressive user acquisition dan liquidity bootstrapping; Points/Gold programs sebagai primary growth lever; compensate untuk late entry ke L2 wars  
Evidence: TGE blog allocation breakdown; Points S1 >500k addresses; Gold to Thruster/Ring/Wasabi/Kaito (HIGH) [Blast Blog TGE, https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event] [Phase 3 EV-004, EV-008/009/010/011]  
Sources: https://blog.blast.io/blast-token-generation-event, Phase 3 EV-004/EV-008/EV-009/EV-010/EV-011

Decision: No protocol revenue transparency (treasury size, composition, yield retention rate undisclosed)  
Reason: Cayman Foundation tidak required public financial disclosure; competitive sensitivity; early stage prioritizes growth over transparency  
Evidence: Phase 5 Treasury/Revenue Model/Revenue History all "tidak diungkap"; no transparency dashboard (HIGH) [Phase 5 Treasury, Revenue Model, Revenue History]  
Sources: Phase 5 Treasury, Revenue Model, Revenue History

Decision: Sequencer revenue (priority fees) flows ke Foundation-operated sequencer — no fee switch ke DAO treasury yet  
Reason: Centralized sequencer architecture; governance not ready for fee management; revenue scale still small vs incentives spend  
Evidence: Docs confirm single sequencer operated by Foundation; EIP-1559 base fee burned on L2, priority fee to sequencer (HIGH) [Blast Docs Sequencer, https://docs.blast.io/architecture/sequencer] [Blast Docs Gas, https://docs.blast.io/developers/gas]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/architecture/sequencer, https://docs.blast.io/developers/gas

Decision: Fund ecosystem via Blast Gold (token emissions dari 28% allocation) bukan grants dalam stablecoin  
Reason: Align protocol success dengan token value; no stablecoin treasury drain; Gold recipients have skin in game via BLAST token  
Evidence: Gold program documented; 28% allocation; protocols receive BLAST token (HIGH) [Blast Docs Gold, https://docs.blast.io/gold] [Phase 6 Distribution: Ecosystem 28%]  
Sources: https://docs.blast.io/gold, Phase 6 Distribution

Decision: No buyback, burn, atau fee switch mechanism untuk BLAST token  
Reason: Fixed supply narrative; governance may propose later; current priority emissions untuk growth  
Evidence: Phase 6 Inflation/Deflation: "Tidak ada native burn mechanism... Tidak ada buyback program resmi" (HIGH) [Phase 6 Inflation/Deflation]  
Sources: Phase 6 Inflation/Deflation

## Ecosystem Decision Pattern

Decision: Deep integration dengan Blur (shared founder, NFT liquidity) sebagai wedge untuk user acquisition  
Reason: Blur has established NFT trader base; founder Tieshun Roquerre bridge kedua ekosistem; NFT finance narrative strong 2023-2024  
Evidence: Phase 2 Entity: Blur (Company external, Application/Liquidity/Distribution); Phase 3 EV-001 founding disclosure mentions Blur integration; Phase 7 Major Integrations: Blur (HIGH) [Phase 2 Blur, Phase 3 EV-001, Phase 7 Major Integrations]  
Sources: Phase 2 Entity: Blur, Phase 3 EV-001, Phase 7 Major Integrations

Decision: Bootstrap core DeFi trio (Thruster DEX, Ring Lending, Wasabi Options) via Gold incentives dalam 60 hari post-mainnet  
Reason: Minimum viable DeFi ecosystem needed untuk TVL retention post-Points S1; concentrated liquidity (Thruster), money market (Ring), derivatives (Wasabi) cover primitives  
Evidence: EV-008/009/010 all Mar-Apr 2024; all receive Gold; Phase 7 Applications list them as core (HIGH) [Phase 3 EV-008/EV-009/EV-010, Phase 7 Applications]  
Sources: Phase 3 EV-008/EV-009/EV-010, Phase 7 Applications

Decision: Integrate Kaito (InfoFi/AI) untuk social analytics dan reward distribution  
Reason: Points S2 mechanic includes social activity; Kaito provides sybil-resistant social signaling; expands "yield" narrative ke attention/social yield  
Evidence: EV-011 May 2024; Phase 7 Applications: Kaito; Phase 8 Narrative: AI/InfoFi tertiary (HIGH) [Phase 3 EV-011, Phase 7 Applications, Phase 8 Narrative Position]  
Sources: Phase 3 EV-011, Phase 7 Applications, Phase 8 Narrative Position

Decision: Rely on third-party bridges (LayerZero, Wormhole, Hyperlane, Orbiter) untuk generic messaging dan fast withdrawals  
Reason: Canonical bridge 7-day delay unacceptable for traders; building native generic messaging delays launch; third-party bridges already multi-chain  
Evidence: Phase 7 Major Integrations: LayerZero/Wormhole/Hyperlane/Orbiter; Phase 4 Known Limitations: "Limited Cross-Chain Messaging (Native)" (HIGH) [Phase 7 Major Integrations, Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations]  
Sources: Phase 7 Major Integrations, Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations

Decision: Support ERC-4337 Account Abstraction via EntryPoint deployment (compatible) bukan native AA  
Reason: EVM equivalence priority; native AA requires custom VM (Starknet, zkSync); ERC-4337 works on any EVM chain via EntryPoint  
Evidence: Phase 4 Execution Environment: "ERC-4337 compatible via EntryPoint"; Phase 7 External Dependencies: ERC-4337 EntryPoint Deployment (MEDIUM) [Phase 4 Execution Environment, Phase 7 External Dependencies]  
Sources: Phase 4 Execution Environment, Phase 7 External Dependencies

Decision: Developer tooling focus pada Foundry/Hardhat compatibility + custom Blast SDK (@blastl2/sdk)  
Reason: Foundry dominant di Ethereum dev; SDK abstracts Blast-specific contracts (native yield, bridge, Points); low friction for existing Ethereum devs  
Evidence: Phase 4 Development Framework: Foundry, Hardhat, Blast SDK, Viem/Ethers; Phase 7 Developer Ecosystem lists these tools (HIGH) [Phase 4 Development Framework, Phase 7 Developer Ecosystem]  
Sources: Phase 4 Development Framework, Phase 7 Developer Ecosystem

## Governance Decision Pattern

Decision: Foundation multisig controls all upgrade keys (L1/L2 proxies) tanpa on-chain timelock verified  
Reason: Speed dan safety untuk early mainnet; DAO infrastructure not ready; standard pattern untuk new L2 (Optimism, Arbitrum started similar)  
Evidence: Phase 4 Security Model: "Admin control oleh Blast Foundation multisig... Tidak ada timelock controller on-chain terverifikasi" (HIGH) [Phase 4 Security Model]  
Sources: Phase 4 Security Model

Decision: Token-weighted governance (1 BLAST = 1 vote) dengan delegation, executed via Foundation multisig  
Reason: Simple, proven model (Compound, Uniswap); delegation enables representation; Foundation execution ensures legal compliance (Cayman entity)  
Evidence: Phase 6 Governance: "1 BLAST = 1 vote (delegatable)"; "Foundation multisig executes passed proposals" (HIGH) [Phase 6 Governance]  
Sources: Phase 6 Governance

Decision: No formal council, committee, atau validator group — Foundation acts as executive pre-DAO  
Reason: Early stage; token distribution just completed; progressive decentralization roadmap projected 2025 (EV-020)  
Evidence: Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem: "Council: Not formally established"; "Committee: Not formally established"; Phase 3 EV-020 DAO Formation projected (HIGH) [Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem, Phase 3 EV-020]  
Sources: Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem, Phase 3 EV-020

Decision: Governance portal (gov.blast.io / Snapshot) not verified live at knowledge cutoff  
Reason: Implementation delay; focus on protocol upgrades (v1.1) dan incentives (S2) first; governance UI lower priority  
Evidence: Phase 6 Governance: "gov.blast.io / Snapshot — not verified live"; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem: "Governance Portal: not verified live" (MEDIUM) [Phase 6 Governance, Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem]  
Sources: Phase 6 Governance, Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Decision: Treasury management opaque — no public addresses, no transparency dashboard, no quarterly reports  
Reason: Cayman Foundation legal structure allows privacy; competitive sensitivity; early stage prioritizes execution over reporting  
Evidence: Phase 5 Treasury: "Current Treasury Size: tidak diungkap"; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "Treasury Concentration / Opaque Treasury Management" (HIGH) [Phase 5 Treasury, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks]  
Sources: Phase 5 Treasury, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks

## Risk Response Pattern

Risk: Centralized sequencer censorship/liveness risk  
Response: No forced inclusion mechanism implemented; no decentralized sequencer roadmap published; acknowledged in docs sebagai "trusted sequencer"  
Evidence: Phase 4 Known Limitations: "Centralized Sequencer (Single)"; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "Single Sequencer Centralization"; Phase 4 Core Components: Sequencer single (HIGH) [Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks, Phase 4 Core Components]  
Sources: Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks, Phase 4 Core Components

Risk: Permissioned proposer/challenger — trust assumption  
Response: No permissionless challenge game live; Foundation operates both; no timeline for permissionless transition  
Evidence: Phase 4 Known Limitations: "Permissioned Proposer & Challenger"; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "Permissioned Proposer and Challenger" (HIGH) [Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks]  
Sources: Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks

Risk: L1 yield source concentration (Lido + MakerDAO)  
Response: No diversification announced; dependency accepted sebagai core architecture; monitor Lido/MakerDAO governance risk  
Evidence: Phase 7 External Dependencies: Lido, MakerDAO Spark critical; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "L1 Yield Source Concentration" (HIGH) [Phase 7 External Dependencies, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks]  
Sources: Phase 7 External Dependencies, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks

Risk: Oracle dependency (Chainlink) untuk yield rate  
Response: No fallback oracle documented; Chainlink industry standard; risk accepted  
Evidence: Phase 7 External Dependencies: Chainlink critical; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "Oracle Dependency (Chainlink)"; Phase 4 Known Limitations: "Native Yield Rate Oracle Dependency" (HIGH) [Phase 7 External Dependencies, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks, Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations]  
Sources: Phase 7 External Dependencies, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks, Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations

Risk: Upgrade key centralization (Foundation multisig)  
Response: No timelock; no emergency pause mechanism public; governance may propose timelock later  
Evidence: Phase 4 Security Model: "Upgrade Control Centralization"; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "Upgrade Key Centralization" (HIGH) [Phase 4 Security Model, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks]  
Sources: Phase 4 Security Model, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks

Risk: Bridge dependency (7-day withdrawal, no fast exit)  
Response: Third-party bridges (Orbiter, LayerZero) supported; canonical bridge only trust-minimized exit  
Evidence: Phase 4 Known Limitations: "7-Day Withdrawal Delay", "Bridge Dependency"; Phase 7 Major Integrations: Orbiter, LayerZero (HIGH) [Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations, Phase 7 Major Integrations]  
Sources: Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations, Phase 7 Major Integrations

Risk: TVL decline post-Points Season 1 (peak $1.48B Mar 2024 → ~$400M Dec 2024)  
Response: Launch Points Season 2 dengan expanded mechanics; Gold incentives ke core protocols; hackathons/grants  
Evidence: Phase 8 Adoption Metrics: TVL peak/decline; Phase 3 EV-014 Season 2 launch; Phase 7 Grant Programs: Gold, Ecosystem Fund (HIGH) [Phase 8 Adoption Metrics, Phase 3 EV-014, Phase 7 Grant Programs]  
Sources: Phase 8 Adoption Metrics, Phase 3 EV-014, Phase 7 Grant Programs

Risk: Investor/team token unlock overhang (36.5% allocation, vesting undisclosed)  
Response: No public vesting schedule; no buyback/burn; rely on token utility (governance, staking, fees) untuk demand  
Evidence: Phase 6 Vesting Schedule: all categories "tidak diketahui"; Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks: "Investor/Team Token Unlock Overhang"; Phase 6 Inflation/Deflation: no buyback (HIGH) [Phase 6 Vesting Schedule, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks, Phase 6 Inflation/Deflation]  
Sources: Phase 6 Vesting Schedule, Phase 7 Ecosystem Risks, Phase 6 Inflation/Deflation

Risk: Regulatory exposure (Cayman Foundation, US persons, token restrictions)  
Response: TGE terms include geographic restrictions; no public legal opinion; Cayman jurisdiction chosen for flexibility  
Evidence: Phase 1 Country: Cayman Islands; Phase 3 EV